  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Banana Ball is a fast-paced, entertainment-focused version of baseball created by the Savannah Bananas, featuring strict rules like a two-hour time limit, no bunting, and fans catching foul balls for outs. Known as \"the greatest show on earth,\" it features dancing players, choreography, and high-energy fan interaction, often compared to the Harlem Globetrotters of baseball. Key 2026 Banana Ball Rules & Features Point System: Points are awarded per inning; the team with the most runs in an inning wins one point, with all runs counting in the final inning. No Bunting/Step Outs: Batters cannot bunt or step out of the box. Fan Outs: Foul balls caught by fans in the stands are counted as outs. Steal First: Batters can steal first base at any time, including on wild pitches or passed balls. Showdown Tiebreaker: If tied after two hours, a \"showdown\" (1-on-1 batter vs. pitcher) resolves the game. Golden Batter: A team can choose any hitter in their lineup to bat once per game. 2026 World Tour & Broadcasts TNT Sports Deal: Starting May 8, 2026, 15 exclusive games will air on truTV and HBO Max, with games at venues like Coors Field, Kauffman Stadium, and Gillette Stadium. The Teams: The tour features the Savannah Bananas, Party Animals, and Texas Tailgaters. Tickets: Tickets are sold via an official lottery system on the Savannah Bananas website. official lottery system For more information, you can explore the official Savannah Bananas website. Savannah Bananas website",
